# The Birth of Stars

Long ago, when the sky was empty and dark, the Night herself grew lonely. She stretched across the heavens in endless silence, watching the sleeping Earth below with no companion to share her vigil.

One evening, the Night wept silver tears of sorrow. As each tear fell, it caught fire from the warmth of her sadness, transforming into brilliant light. These tears scattered across the vast darkness, each one burning with its own eternal flame.

The Earth saw this spectacle and called up to her: "Beautiful Night, why do you weep?"

"I am alone," Night replied, "with nothing but emptiness to keep me company."

"But look what your tears have created!" said Earth. "You have filled the darkness with ten thousand points of light. They dance and shimmer, each one unique. You are no longer alone—you are surrounded by your own children."

